WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.050
A payments bug comes in.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.320
Customers with accented letters in their address

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.140
can't pay.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.880
One engineer tells an agent,

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.040
there's a bug for international users,

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:13.900
take a look.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.100
It returns a patch that strips every

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.850
accent from every address.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.460
Worse than the bug.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.360
A second engineer pastes in the error

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.000
log,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:22.800
the trace,

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.720
the gateway docs,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.320
and the three files involved.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.530
The fix is four lines.

00:00:28.307 --> 00:00:29.167
Same model.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:30.057
Same agent.

00:00:30.107 --> 00:00:32.227
What changed was what the agent could

00:00:32.227 --> 00:00:32.687
see.

00:00:32.687 --> 00:00:34.587
That's why the most important skill here

00:00:34.587 --> 00:00:35.587
isn't prompting.

00:00:35.587 --> 00:00:37.297
It's context engineering:

00:00:37.607 --> 00:00:39.907
curating everything that lands in the model's

00:00:39.907 --> 00:00:40.757
window.

00:00:41.259 --> 00:00:43.049
Think of the window as a workbench.

00:00:43.279 --> 00:00:44.379
Space is limited,

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:46.199
so you lay out only what this

00:00:46.199 --> 00:00:47.099
task needs.

00:00:47.099 --> 00:00:49.079
But the real skill is designing the

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:49.499
workshop,

00:00:49.499 --> 00:00:52.039
with clear structure and labelled drawers,

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:53.759
so the agent can pull the right

00:00:53.759 --> 00:00:55.389
tool off the wall itself.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:58.500
Context reaches an agent on a ladder.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:00:59.720
At level zero,

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:01.210
you describe the problem in your own

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:01.810
words,

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.450
and the detail gets lost.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:04.630
At level one,

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.410
you paste the raw stack trace.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.090
Better,

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:08.840
but tomorrow you paste it again.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:10.060
At level two,

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.590
the agent can run the test and

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:12.930
read the trace itself,

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.730
and you add only what no tool

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:15.530
can find:

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:16.270
your intent,

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.640
and your constraints.

00:01:18.604 --> 00:01:20.694
That's infrastructure versus injection.

00:01:21.324 --> 00:01:23.224
Infrastructure is set up once and pays

00:01:23.224 --> 00:01:24.544
off in every session:

00:01:24.544 --> 00:01:25.674
tool access,

00:01:25.724 --> 00:01:27.594
integrations with your error tracker,

00:01:27.724 --> 00:01:29.064
a navigable repo,

00:01:29.064 --> 00:01:30.694
an instruction file.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.904
Injection is what you paste by hand.

00:01:32.904 --> 00:01:34.364
When you paste the same thing a

00:01:34.364 --> 00:01:35.084
third time,

00:01:35.084 --> 00:01:35.934
promote it.

00:01:36.542 --> 00:01:37.832
And more is not better.

00:01:37.962 --> 00:01:39.562
Every token costs twice,

00:01:39.562 --> 00:01:41.292
in money and in attention.

00:01:41.322 --> 00:01:43.102
Details buried in the middle get less

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:43.542
weight,

00:01:43.542 --> 00:01:45.912
and quality degrades as the input grows.

00:01:46.082 --> 00:01:47.642
It's called context rot,

00:01:47.642 --> 00:01:49.602
and a bigger window doesn't cure it.

00:01:49.602 --> 00:01:50.912
Before adding anything,

00:01:50.922 --> 00:01:51.482
ask:

00:01:51.482 --> 00:01:53.802
will the agent decide differently because it

00:01:53.802 --> 00:01:54.652
saw this?

00:01:55.293 --> 00:01:57.373
Long sessions fill up with noise,

00:01:57.373 --> 00:01:59.383
compact them into a short brief,

00:01:59.513 --> 00:02:01.053
have the agent keep notes in a

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:01.833
file,

00:02:01.833 --> 00:02:04.073
send big explorations to a sub -agent

00:02:04.073 --> 00:02:05.903
that returns only the conclusion,

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.493
then work in phases,

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:08.343
research,

00:02:08.473 --> 00:02:09.273
plan,

00:02:09.273 --> 00:02:10.123
implement,

00:02:10.153 --> 00:02:11.623
each in a fresh window.

00:02:12.408 --> 00:02:13.588
When a session ends,

00:02:13.588 --> 00:02:14.918
its window is gone.

00:02:14.988 --> 00:02:16.458
So commit often,

00:02:16.468 --> 00:02:17.458
keep the notes,

00:02:17.548 --> 00:02:19.128
and put what's permanent in the instruction

00:02:19.128 --> 00:02:19.908
file.

00:02:19.908 --> 00:02:21.108
Your code,

00:02:21.108 --> 00:02:22.788
your repo and your docs are all

00:02:22.788 --> 00:02:23.808
context now.

00:02:23.808 --> 00:02:24.698
Next up:

00:02:24.748 --> 00:02:25.568
guardrails,

00:02:25.568 --> 00:02:26.348
trust,

00:02:26.348 --> 00:02:27.618
and sandboxes.
